    <statement><p>Evaluate the integral:</p>
<p><me>\int_{0}^{t} (9 s {\bf i} + 3 s^2 {\bf j} + 7 {\bf k}) \,ds</me> 
Answer :  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>{\bf i} \, +</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>{\bf j} \, +</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/><m>{\bf k}</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.5t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1t^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int_{0}^{t} 9 s \,ds = \left.\frac{9}{2} s^{2}\right|_{0}^{t}=
 \frac{9}{2} t^2</me>
<me>\int_{0}^{t} 3 s^2 \,ds = \left.\frac{3}{3} s^{3}\right|_0^t=
 1 t^3</me>
<me>\left.\int_{0}^{t} 7 \,ds = 7 s\right|_0^t=7 t</me>
Hence,



<me>\int_{0}^{t} (9 s \bf{i}\it + 3 s^2 \bf{j}\it + 7 \bf{k}\it) \,ds = \left(\int_{0}^{t} 9 s \,ds\right) \bf{i}\it + \left(\int_{0}^{t} 3 s^2 \,ds\right) \bf{j}\it + \left(\int_{0}^{t} 7 \,ds\right) \bf{k}\it</me>


 
<me>=\left(\frac{9}{2} t^2\right)\bf{i}\it + \left(1 t^3\right) \bf{j}\it + \left(7 t\right) \bf{k}\it</me> 



</solution>
